## 6. Usage

```bash
cd ~/wal

# Build shard logs (one checksummed record per line, appended):
./walrec.sh mkrec 0 T1 s0 PREPARE - - -  >> s0.log
./walrec.sh mkrec 1 T1 s0 COMMIT  - 0 -  >> s0.log
./walrec.sh mkrec 0 T1 s1 PREPARE - - -  >> s1.log
./walrec.sh mkrec 1 T1 s1 COMMIT  - 0 -  >> s1.log

# Validate only; committed txns in commit order on stdout:
./walrec.sh --check s0.log s1.log

# Recover into a directory (repaired logs + state + JSON report, all atomic):
./walrec.sh --out recovered s0.log s1.log
cat recovered/recovered.state
jq . recovered/report.json

# Optionally truncate torn tails in the inputs (idempotent):
./walrec.sh --out recovered --in-place s0.log s1.log
```

Exit codes: `0` recovered, `1` impossible history / corrupt WAL, `2` usage/I/O.

